---
title: Owned compute, independent supervision, durable results
---
flowchart LR
  accTitle: PodVigil architecture
  accDescr: A local controller and detached watchdog preserve each attempt's ledger. The wait command reads a ledger without cloud access or changing the job. Optional capacity retries require a definite no-capacity answer and verified absence, then poll the catalog before another attempt. The controller manages an owned Runpod Secure Cloud Pod through the provider API. Inside the Pod a privileged guard supervises an unprivileged workload and snapshots local outputs to a private network volume. A local backup is verified before that volume can be deleted.

  subgraph LOCAL["YOUR COMPUTER"]
    direction TB
    CLI["podvigil command<br/>Plan and launch<br/>Inspect and recover"] --> CTRL["Controller<br/>Ownership and cost<br/>Verified capacity retries"]
    CLI --> WAIT["wait JOB<br/>Read local ledger<br/>Job unaffected"]
    CTRL --> WATCH["Detached watchdog<br/>Independent deadline and recovery"]
    CTRL -.-> LEDGER[("Attempt ledger<br/>Ownership, cleanup<br/>Outcome evidence")]
    WATCH -.-> LEDGER
    WAIT -.->|"read only"| LEDGER
  end

  API["Runpod API<br/>Catalog and price<br/>Secure Cloud only"]

  subgraph POD["OWNED SECURE CLOUD POD"]
    direction TB
    GUARD["Privileged guard and supervisor<br/>Deadline, snapshot and self-deletion"]
    WORK["Unprivileged workload<br/>No account or S3 credentials"]
    DISK[("Local Pod outputs")]
    GUARD --> WORK --> DISK
  end

  subgraph RESULTS["RESULT RECOVERY"]
    direction TB
    VOLUME[("Owned network volume<br/>Survives Pod termination")]
    VOLUME -->|"S3 retrieval after compute is gone"| BACKUP[("Verified local backup<br/>Artifacts and checksums")]
    BACKUP --> AUDIT["Audit all volume objects<br/>Then delete owned storage"]
  end

  LOCAL -->|"catalog reads<br/>create, verify, delete"| API
  API --> POD
  POD -->|"supervisor snapshot"| RESULTS

  classDef primary fill:#eaf2ff,stroke:#3864a2,color:#142b49,stroke-width:2px;
